WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.602
Growth can build on growth.

2
00:00:01.722 --> 00:00:07.783
Compounding means interest or returns can apply to earlier interest or returns as well as the starting amount.

3
00:00:08.303 --> 00:00:09.719
A simple first year.

4
00:00:09.839 --> 00:00:16.445
At a hypothetical 5% yearly rate, $1,000 becomes $1,050 after one year.

5
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:20.011
The next year builds on $1,050.

6
00:00:20.131 --> 00:00:28.525
At the same hypothetical rate, another $52.50 brings the balance to $1,102.50.

7
00:00:29.053 --> 00:00:30.493
It can work against you.

8
00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:32.679
Debt interest can also compound.

9
00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:36.294
Rates, fees, payments, and terms affect the result.

10
00:00:36.814 --> 00:00:38.764
Examples are not forecasts.

11
00:00:38.884 --> 00:00:41.682
Investment returns vary and may be negative.

12
00:00:41.802 --> 00:00:44.891
Compare assumptions before using any growth projection.

